Contract notes
--------------
* Google's flatPath expands reserved resource templates to individual segments;
  callers can use IDs or validated project/location/parent-scoped resource names.
* String-encoded protobuf int64/uint64 values remain strings; bytes remain
  base64 JSON strings. Timestamp schemas use date-time. Field masks remain strings.
* Explicit Required. field behavior is retained. readOnly fields are omitted
  from request forms. Unknown schema constructs fail normalization.
* Known long-running metadata/results are typed alternatives. protobuf Any
  retains an open alternative for future service types; other document fields
  retain their complete declared nested types.
* process-document consolidates processor and processor-version processing.
  Processor types use the paginated stable processorTypes.list operation in
  place of the duplicate fetchProcessorTypes endpoint.
* Stable operations are preferred; beta-only dataset/import actions are named
  explicitly and use v1beta3 paths and types.
* Human review is excluded because HITL is deprecated:
  https://docs.cloud.google.com/document-ai/docs/deprecation
* Legacy projects.operations.get and operations.delete are excluded. Current
  jobs use projects.locations.operations; its supported contract has get, list,
  and cancel, but no delete. Cancellation is asynchronous, not deletion.
  https://docs.cloud.google.com/document-ai/docs/access-control/iam-permissions

Every source declaration has a mapping or explicit decision in the inventory.
